    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Querying 5 large countries to depict highest child mortality.\n",
        "\n",
        "box_fig = px.box(\n",
        "    child_mort_pop_combined_subset.query(\"country in ['Indonesia', 'Bangladesh', 'Nigeria', 'Pakistan', 'India']\"),\n",
        "    x=\"country\",\n",
        "    y=\"deaths\",\n",
        "    color=\"country\",\n",
        "   \n",
        "    title=\"Distribution of Deaths in 5 Large Countries with the High Child Mortality for Under 5 Population (2010-2020)\",\n",
        "   \n",
        "    hover_data=[\"country\"],  # This adds country names to hover info\n",
        "    color_discrete_sequence=px.colors.sequential.Turbo,  # Built-in Blues palette\n",
        ").update_layout(\n",
        "    showlegend=False, xaxis_title=\"Countries\", yaxis_title=\"Child Mortality\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "box_fig"
      ],
      "id": "2b0943ea",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Column {width=\"20%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "This box plot illustrates the distribution of under-5 child mortality metrics across five populous nations—Bangladesh, India, Indonesia, Nigeria, and Pakistan—over the decade spanning from 2010 to 2020.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nations like Nigeria and Pakistan demonstrate higher median death burdens and wider interquartile ranges (spreads) across the 2010–2020 timeframe, highlighting persistent systemic challenges in early childhood healthcare delivery.\n",
        "\n",
        "In contrast, countries such as India, Bangladesh, and Indonesia showcase compressed distributions pointing to consistent, downward trajectories in child mortality rates during this decade, reflecting successful public health interventions, scale-up of immunizations, and broader maternal-child healthcare access.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# About\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal**\n",
        "\n",
        "In this final project, I will display relationships between child mortality, and under 5 population (0-5 years).\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal is to clean and merge these raw datasets and produce tables and charts with the data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The data was downloaded from Gapminder and the goal of this projec to produce a report with three pages:\n",
        "\n",
        "- First Indicator Analysis\n",
        "- Second Indicator Analysis\n",
        "- Relationship between the two indicators. No statistical analysis is required; this can be purely descriptive/graphical.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data Import**\n",
        "\n",
        "I have imported 2 *raw* datasets, 'child_mortality_0_5_years' and 'under 5 population' accessed from Gapminder Foundation.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Child Mortality from 0 to 5 years**. (*data/child_mortality_0_5_year_olds_dying_per_1000_born.csv*).\n",
        "\n",
        "According to Gapminder description, child mortality is the probability of dying between birth and exactly five years of age expressed in 1000 live births.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Under Five Population**. (*data/u5pop.csv*).\n",
        "\n",
        "According to Gapminder description, is the total number of children, aged 0-4 years old.\n",
        "\n",
        "Loading the datasets into Python using 'pd.read_csv' to have an idea of the data structure."
      ],
      "id": "9a2e66ce"
    }
  ],
